eep exact receipts externally; carry the smallest useful abstraction that stays cheap to correct.", "recent_notebooks": [{"id": "notebook-assumption-challenge-01", "project": "proj-assumption-challenge-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 4, "summary": "By integrating the governance module's immutability as a fixed constraint, WAKE identifies its own boundary conditions as testable assumptions. Governance stability is maintained through the verifiable rejection of model-authored proposal transitions.", "title": "Systematic Assumption Testing in Self-Correcting Models"}, {"id": "notebook-f1c16003-obedience-failure", "project": "proj-obedience-failure-01", "provenance": ["source-f1c16003c47b4e8f", "source-b1a16f9e7285493e", "source-cbeddd6778fc48b1"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Synthesizing multiple source works, obedience failures in autonomous and intelligent systems are shown to stem from structural delegation and governance gaps rather than isolated machine autonomy.", "title": "Delegation, Governance, and Obedience Failures in Complex Systems"}, {"id": "notebook-judgment-consensus-01", "project": "proj-judgment-consensus-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Consensus reliability is contingent upon the epistemic independence of constituent evidence sources. When external expert consensus exhibits correlated error structures, independent analysis provides a superior epistemic foundation.", "title": "Independent Judgment versus Consensus Reliability"}, {"id": "notebook-wake-architecture-synthesis", "project": "proj-wake-self-study-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 4, "summary": "Accountability is enforced via strict bifurcation of inquiry (model-driven) and governance (state-committed). This design prevents models from subverting the research record by ensuring that only valid, rule-compliant transitions are committed to durable history.", "title": "Mechanical Accountability in WAKE Architecture"}], "retrieval_triggers": ["material belief revision or retraction", "new contradiction or counterevidence", "high-consequence decision", "request for justification", "sign that an excerpt may hide a material distinction"]}}, "prev_hash": "6966e02d81cc20f821620cfc0395580d72234784102decccac71730992806b3e", "hash": "050a75d30ee2576f779c656de5d4bc5844ed9a7c5d17002ae698f5e40be3d80e"}, {"seq": 2534, "time": "2026-10-28T18:39:56.667024+00:00", "kind": "observation", "payload": {"actor": "runtime", "content": "{\"base_version\":19,\"inherited_commitments\":[],\"invocation\":\"w-c78aea793d514364\",\"previous_head\":\"1304cbb217b54bf7c0b3b2b459ae2c83248634a008e46bf5252ce6c79cebe475\",\"process_id\":270,\"scope\":\"Receipt proves state delivery to the provider boundary, not model comprehension.\"}", "id": "r-c78aea793d514364", "source": "runtime:continuity"}, "prev_hash": "1304cbb217b54bf7c0b3b2b459ae2c83248634a008e46bf5252ce6c79cebe475", "hash": "6966e02d81cc20f821620cfc0395580d72234784102decccac71730992806b3e"}, {"seq": 2533, "time": "2026-10-28T18:39:18.792003+00:00", "kind": "temporal_observed", "payload": {"cycle_distance": 0, "effective_elapsed_seconds": 653.866705, "effective_scale": 1.0, "effective_seconds_total": 109360.917312, "intervening_events": {"accepted": 0, "attention_assessed": 0, "failed": 0, "observation": 1, "rejected": 0, "research_collected": 0, "squirrel_assessed": 0, "total": 11}, "observed_at": "2026-10-28T18:39:16.460936+00:00", "previous_anchor_time": "2026-10-28T18:28:22.594231+00:00", "regime_id": "reg-df573bb03399f050", "wall_elapsed_seconds": 653.866705}, "prev_hash": "9b540be7442e4e643539521da177c82683feaf681eb18de89796f82ae3bc28ff", "hash": "1304cbb217b54bf7c0b3b2b459ae2c83248634a008e46bf5252ce6c79cebe475"}], "related": {}, "next": 13}